  "title": "XML: fix issue about parsing encoding attribute when standalone attribute exists",
  "description": "This MR will close issue #19485.\n\nThe reason is the default the quantifiers ```(.+)``` of regex pattern are \"greedy\", that is, they match as much as possible. So, the xml\n the encoding value of declaration ```<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"GB18030\" standalone=\"yes\"?>``` will be parsed as ```GB18030\" standalone=\"yes```. Now, we make the sub pattern parsing the value of encoding and version attributes in 'ungreedy' mode.\n\nAt the same time, this commit fixed a bug introduced from MR !12306 that causes the encoding attribute unable to be parsed at all because missing '1' in ```{,50}```, that should be  ```{1,50})```.\n\nThe test result after applying this change:\n\n![ok](/uploads/bcd1e77f76b98310f85422a3314f20a4/ok.png)\n\nThis change can be cherry-picked to release-4.2.0. (Perhaps it should be cherry-picked with the change of the MR !12306 at the same time)",
  "state": "merged",
